 A minor/major spoiler, depending on how you look at it...

1) Upon playing more, I have found stuff up to +8.  The random number
   generator "rne" generates a random number with an exponential
   probablity curve, so ungodly high numbers are infinitesimally
   possible...

2) You got whaled on with AC -22 because the program, upon sensing that
   you have negative AC, gives you a new AC every time you're attacked,
   which is a random number from your "real" AC up to 0.  So that frost
   giant could have been attacking AC 0 at times, which is like the
   broad side of a barn to that bastard.  I took out that rediculous
   line of code...  Ideally, though, the monster should have a 1/20
   chance of hitting *anything*, like D&D...

